From e97b99dcfd0e217c40f106397d397c55a14ccce9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kuzma30 <kuzemkoa@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:10:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/25] Modeling Algorithms - Close a fillet of a concave edge
 in the tangent plane at its end

FreeCAD issue 20085, a cube of 20 with fillets of radius 6 and a square
hole of 8 x 8 whose walls go along the tangent lines of the fillets of
the cube: the fillet of a vertical (concave) edge of the hole, alone or
with the lower edges on both sides of it (Edge33, Edge42 and Edge57 in
FreeCAD), failed with faulty vertices at the ends of that edge
("BRep_API: command not done").

At an end of the vertical edge the fillet ends at the end vertex of its
spine. Its last section lies in the plane of the top (bottom) of the
cube, removed by the hole, and so do the edges of the walls from the
section to the vertex: the fillets of the cube beyond them are tangent
to that plane along them.

- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformCapInTangentPlane: in that configuration the end
  is closed by a planar cap in that plane, bounded by the section and by
  the edges of the walls from the section to the vertex, built as a
  corner by ChFi3d_Builder::CapInSectionPlane.
- ChFi3d_Builder::CapInSectionPlane: the side of the cap opposite to the
  arc through the vertex is either the line on the other support (as
  before) or the arc of that side through the vertex. The orientation of
  the cap is computed from the orientation of the arc on the face beyond
  it, which must be the opposite of its orientation in the cap.

The vertical edge alone is valid for r = 0.5 to 2.9 with tolerance 1e-4
and adds r * r * (1 - pi / 4) * 20 (17.168 mm3 with r = 2). With the
lower edges on both sides it is valid; their corner is a patch
(tolerance 0.014 with r = 1, 0.07 with r = 2).

New DRAW test bugs/modalg_8/fillet_rounded_cube_square_hole_concave_edge
and GTest
BRepFilletAPI_MakeFilletTest.SquareHoleInRoundedCube_ConcaveEdgeEndsInTangentPlane.

